build: 2026-07-01 v10.77.2 (New looks · unified Tools · audio route hardening · projection)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie (deployed via deploy branch)
notesT: This build ships a batch of upgrades — all compile-verified via the Xcode gate.
  NEW VISUAL LOOKS: three immersive looks join the Look strip (and the Blend-with strip):
  Aurora (soft northern-lights curtains), Lissajous (tone-driven woven figures), and Depth
  Caustics (layered light with depth). Open the fullscreen visual → Look → pick one; blend
  any two.
  TOOLS REACHABILITY: the bottom "Tools" menu and the Tools grid now come from ONE list, so
  every tool is reachable from both — the quick menu previously lacked Drum Samples, Import
  MIDI, Live Colabo and MIDI/Health; they're all there now.
  AUDIO ROUTE HARDENING: when the rPPG camera switches the audio route mid-session (to
  44.1 kHz), the capture tap is now re-installed so any recording/export keeps the correct
  pitch/tempo even if the route flips while playing — a follow-through on the 10.77.1 fix.
  PROJECTION: the fullscreen visual is a projector surface (chrome-free, screen stays awake,
  status bar hidden) — mirror it to a beamer/TV via Control Center → Screen Mirroring
  (AirPlay). A hint in the visual's control panel now points this out. (Dedicated dual-screen
  is a later cycle.)
  Test 10.77.2: fullscreen visual → try Aurora/Lissajous/Depth + blend; open the bottom Tools
  menu and confirm Drum Samples/Import MIDI/MIDI-Health are listed; with rPPG running, record
  a clip and confirm the pitch still matches live; AirPlay-mirror the visual to a screen.
